owth hole understated.\n  2) SBC/dilution still 4.8% of revenue.\n  3) AI revenue not separately disclosed.\nPre-mortem: If SAP fails 5 years from now, cause will be\n  (most likely) post-2027 revenue collapse to <2% growth AND\n  FCF margin stuck <22%; early warning = CCB growth <15%.\n```\n\n---\n\n## SECTION 12 \u2014 FINAL EXECUTION OPINION\n\n| Decision attribute | Value |\n|---|---|\n| **Action** | **HOLD / ACCUMULATE ON WEAKNESS \u2014 DO NOT CHASE AT $219** |\n| **Conviction** | **10/15 (High-lower half)** |\n| **Fair value** | **E[P] $243 (50% CI $222\u2013268, 80% CI $170\u2013310)** |\n| **MoS at current price** | **9.8% \u2014 LIMITED** |\n| **Target weight** | **4% at T0; 6% maximum below $195** |\n| **Entry plan** | 1% at \u2264$210; 2% at \u2264$195; 2% at \u2264$175; final 1% at \u2264$160 |\n| **Trim plan** | Sell 50% above $280; exit all but 1% runner above $310 |\n| **Kelly verdict** | Zero position at T0; practical allocation justified only by conviction in CCB-converted revenue |\n| **Horizon** | 3\u20135 years (not 12-month rating) |\n| **KPIs to monitor** | CCB growth \u226520%; Cloud ERP Suite \u226525%; FCF margin ex-SBC \u226521%; SBC/Rev \u22645%; op-margin guide \u226530% |\n\n**Closing rationale:**\nSAP is a fortress-quality compounder with a contracted-revenue backbone (CCB \u20ac22.9B, +27% [Actual]) and a net-cash balance sheet. The stock is *not cheap*: at $219 it prices 27x trailing earnings and ~24x adjusted owner earnings, with only a 9.8% margin of safety to my expected value of $243. The 2025\u20132027 growth window is real and contracted; the post-2027 reversion is real and largely unpriced in both directions. The entry discipline is therefore the entire game: **accumulate on weakness into $195\u2013170, hold through the 2027 ECC conversion, and trim aggressively into $280+.** This is a compounder to own on sale, not to chase at market.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u255