 population.\n3. **Switch cost depth**: S/4HANA + RISE + Business AI sits at the core of regulated financial reporting; replacement cycles are 5\u201310 years, unlike peer software categories where the AI disruption base rate was formed.\n4. **Pricing power demonstrated**: Q2 2026 cloud gross margin held at 74.6% non-IFRS [Actual] despite scale-up.\n\nNo deviation above 1.5\u00d7 \u2192 no red flag. If success probability exceeded 75% (1.5\u00d750%), re-evaluation would be mandatory.\n\n**Step 1.5-3. Base-rate shock check**: Pass. My success probabilities: Cloud AI conversion 65% vs base 45%, ratio 1.44\u00d7 < 1.5\u00d7 \u2014 no mandatory re-evaluation.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n\u25a0 SECTION 2. BUSINESS QUALITY (Buffett + Lynch)\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n\n**Step 2-1. Business understanding** (3 sentences):\nSAP sells mission-critical enterprise software: ERP (S/4HANA), financial management, supply chain, HCM, spend management, and Business AI, delivered mostly as cloud subscriptions (57% of revenue). Customers cannot operate without it \u2014 it runs the financial books of 17,000+ large organizations \u2014 and switching is a multi-year, multi-million-dollar project. The strategy transitions on-premise customers to RISE with SAP / S/4HANA Cloud, monetizing the installed base as recurring cloud revenue with AI as an accelerator.\nUnderstandability: **High**.\n\n**Step 2-2. Moat assessment + dynamics**:\n\n| Moat type | Score (0\u20133) | Direction |\n|---|---|---|\n| Intangible assets (brand, patents) | 3 | Stable \u2014 enterprise brand trusted for 50 years |\n| Switching costs | 3 | Widening \u2014 S/4HANA + AI agents deepen workflow integration |\n| Network effects | 2 | Widening \u2014 43,338 vendor-published implementations, partner ecosystem (ERP Research) [Estimate] |\n| Cost advantage | 1 | Stable \u2014 not a cost leader, but services delivered via partner ecosystem |\n| Economies of scale | 3 | Widening \u2014 R&D budget ~\u20ac5\u20136B/yr [Assumption] cannot be matched by ERP mid-market rivals |\n| Regulatory barriers | 2 | Stable \u2014 audited financial reporting, FEDRAMP, public-sector contracts; EU scrutiny is a minor negative |\n| Data moat | 3 | Widening \u2014 LLM training on global business process data across 17,000+ customers |\n\n**Moat score: 17/21 \u2014 Fortress** (upper end), direction **Widening**, partially offset by Oracle's HCM/financials inroads [Estimate \u2014 Futurum/ERP Research]. Net moat trend: **Widening**.\n\n**Step 2-3. Lynch classification**: **Stalwart-plus** \u2014 total revenue growth 8\u201311% (FY2025 +8%, +11% cc) with a cloud segment growing at 23\u201326%. Stalwart checkpoints: P/E vs growth \u2014 trailing P/E 27.0 vs EPS growth 17.6% consensus \u2192 PEG ~1.5\u20131.8, slightly above the classic <1.5 threshold; the offset is the quality of revenue (86% predictable) [Actual \u2014 vendor/press release].\n\n**Step 2-4. Financial strength scorecard**:\n\n| Metric | Value | Tag/Period |\n|---|---|---|\n| Revenue growth, FY2025 | +8% reported / +11% cc | [Actual \u2014 Q4 2025 release] |\n| 3-yr revenue CAGR (FY22\u2192FY25) | ~6% (from ~\u20ac30.9B base; exact base not retrieved \u2014 [Estimate]) | [Estimate] |\n| Non-IFRS operating margin FY2025 | 28.3% (\u20ac10.419B / \u20ac36.800B) | [Actual \u2014 Arithmetic] |\n| Non-IFRS operating margin Q2 2026 | 27.8% | [Actual \u2014 Q2 2026 release] |\n| EPS growth (basic IFRS FY25 vs FY24) | +100% (\u20ac6.28 vs \u20ac2.68) \u2014 distorted by one-offs; non-IFRS EPS +36% (\u20ac6.15 vs \u20ac4.53) | [Actual] |\n| ROE | 18.3% | [Actual \u2014 vendor] |\n| FCF margin | 22.4% (\u20ac8.24B / \u20ac36.80B) | [Actual \u2014 Arithmetic] |\n| OCF | \u20ac9.16B | [Actual] |\n| Net debt | \u2248 \u20ac0 net cash per vendor ($9.7B cash vs $8.8B debt) + ~\u20ac3B leases [Unconfirmed] \u2192 **net debt ~\u20ac2\u20133B** | [Estimate] |\n\n**Judgment: Excellent.**\n\n**Step 2-5. Capital allocation scorecard (0\u20133 each, /15)**:\n1. **Buyback efficiency**: 2 \u2014 New \u20ac10B program, 16.3M shares at avg \u20ac161.16 (below current \u20ac188) [Actual]; SBC partially offsets (est. \u20ac1.9\u20132.1B/yr [Estimate])\n2. **M&A track record**: 1 \u2014 Reltio, Dremio, Prior Labs, Supabase are bolt-ons, but 5-year M&A ROIC not proven; Dremio/Prior Labs dilutive to 2026 OP (>\u20ac100M) [Actual]\n3. **Capex efficiency**: 3 \u2014 Capex only ~\u20ac0.9B on \u20ac36.8B revenue (2.5%); hyperscaler/partner capacity used instead of owned data centers; incremental ROIC very high [Estimate]\n4. **Rationality of mix**: 2 \u2014 Balanced buybacks, dividend, and cloud/AI reinvestment; slight concern on small-speculative AI acquisitions\n5. **Guidance accuracy**: 3 \u2014 FY2025 revenue met, non-IFRS OP and FCF exceeded [Actual]; Q2 2026 beat [Actual]; 2026 OP guidance revised only due to M&A dilution\n- Total: **11/15 \u2014 Good**\n- Insider ownership bonus: 0 (insider 0.0% per pack; no insider data)\n- Final: **11/15**\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n\u25a0 SECTION 2.5. INTANGIBLES-ADJUSTED FINANCIALS\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n\n**Step 2.5-1. R&D capitalization** [Assumption-heavy]:\nR&D expense FY2025 estimated at **\u20ac5.9B** [Assumption \u2014 FY2024 was ~\u20ac5.7B; growth continued; not retrieved]. Capitalized treatment (3-year amortization, straight-line):\n- Adjusted operating income \u2248 non-IFRS OP \u20ac10.42B + (R&D \u2212 amortization \u2248 \u20ac0.45B) \u2248 **\u20ac10.87B** [Estimate]\n- Adjusted invested capital \u2248 equity \u20ac30.7B [pack FY2017 \u2014 stale] \u2014 better: current equity \u2248 \u20ac25\u201328B [Estimate: vendor equity $30.7B/1.1662 \u2248 \u20ac26.3B] + net debt \u20ac2.3B + unamortized R&D (~\u20ac15B) \u2248 **\u20ac43B** [Assumption]\n- **Adjusted ROIC \u2248 10.87 \u00d7 (1\u22120.29) / 43 \u2248 18%** [Estimate] vs GAAP ROE 18.3% \u2014 gap small because brand/enterprise intangibles already expensed; no 5%+ divergence needs explanation.\n\n**Step 2.5-2. SBC treatment**: Vendor SBC $1.916B (= ~\u20ac1.64B at 1.1662) [Actual \u2014 vendor, period unreliable]; annual SBC likely \u20ac1.7\u20132.1B [Estimate]. Adjusted FCF FY2025 = \u20ac8.24B \u2212 \u20ac1.9B = **\u20ac6.3\u20136.5B** [Estimate]. Consistent with FCF/OCF conversion still ~70% \u2014 acceptable for a subscription business.\n\n**Step 2.5-3. Operating leases**: Not mapped in pack; [Unconfirmed]. I add a blanket **\u20ac3.0B** debt-equivalent [Assumption] to the EV bridge. Coverage remains ~10\u00d7+; immaterial to the conclusion.\n\n**Step 2.5-4. Brand/data assets**: Not valued separately; the data moat is embedded in the margin forecast (cloud GM 74\u201375% and 32% operating margin by 2030).\n\n**Step 2.5-6. Owner earnings (Buffett)**: \nOwner Earnings = IFRS NI \u20ac7.49B + D&A ~\u20ac2.0B [Estimate] \u2212 maintenance capex ~\u20ac0.6B [Assumption] \u2212 \u0394WC ~0 \u2248 **\u20ac8.9B** [Estimate]. This exceeds the dividend+buyback cash outflow (~\u20ac2.5B dividend + \u20ac5B/yr buyback) by a wide margin \u2014 owner-earnings coverage strong.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n\u25a0 SECTION 3. VALUATION \u2014 ENGINE 1 (DCF + MULTIPLES)\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n\n**Step 3-1. Discount-rate derivation (WACC)**:\n- Risk-free rate: German 10Y Bund **3.18%** [Actual \u2014 Trading Economics, 2026-08-25]\n- Equity risk premium: **5.5%** [Assumption \u2014 Damodaran-style global mature-market ERP]\n- Beta: vendor raw **0.757** [Actual \u2014 vendor, window unknown]; adjusted to **0.80** [Assumption \u2014 small uplift for AI-disruption and Middle East uncertainty]\n- Cost of equity = 3.18% + 0.80 \u00d7 5.5% = **7.58%**\n- Cost of debt: Bund + 80bps = ~4.0% pre-tax; after-tax \u00d7(1\u22120.29) = **2.84%** [Assumption]\n- Weights: E = \u20ac216.9B market cap; D \u2248 \u20ac2.3B net debt incl. leases [Assumption] \u2192 D/(D+E) = 1.05%\n- **WACC = 0.9895 \u00d7 7.58% + 0.0105 \u00d7 2.84% = 7.53% \u2248 7.5%** [Assumption-labeled blended estimate]\n\nSensitivity WACC \u00b150bps is shown in the Tornado (Step 3-X).\n\n**Step 3-2. Forecast (explicit, per-year, EUR billions)** \u2014 all 2026\u20132027 figures are company-guidance-anchored; 2028\u20132030 are [Assumption] and dominate the uncertainty:\n\n| FY | Revenue | Growth (reported) | Non-IFRS OP margin | Non-IFRS OP | Tax @29% | D&A | Capex | \u0394WC | OCF | FCF |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 2025A | 36.80 | +8% | 28.3% | 10.42 | 3.02 | ~2.0 | 0.92 | \u2014 | 9.16 | 8.24 |\n| 2026E | 40.40 | +9.8% | 29.5% | 11.90 | 3.45 | 2.10 | 1.10 | \u22120.20 | 11.10 | 10.00 |\n| 2027E | 45.60 | +12.9% | 30.8% | 14.05 | 4.07 | 2.40 | 1.30 | +0.30 | 12.08 | 10.78 |\n| 2028E | 50.20 | +10.0% | 31.2% | 15.66 | 4.54 | 2.70 | 1.50 | +0.30 | 13.52 | 12.02 |\n| 2029E | 54.60 | +8.8% | 31.7% | 17.30 | 5.02 | 2.90 | 1.70 | +0.30 | 14.88 | 13.18 |\n| 2030E | 58.80 | +7.7% | 32.2% | 18.94 | 5.48 | 3.10 | 1.90 | +0.30 | 16.22 | 14.32 |\n\n**Driver sourcing \u2014 audit trail**:\n- **2026 revenue and FCF**: SAP official guidance \u2014 cloud \u20ac25.8\u201326.2B (+23\u201325% cc), cloud+software \u20ac36.3\u201336.8B cc, FCF ~\u20ac10B actual [Actual \u2014 Q2 2026 statement]. I used \u20ac40.4B total revenue (guidance's \"similar levels as 2025\" \u2248 10.6% cc, minus 1.5pp FX drag from EUR at 1.17 vs 1.13 assumption) [Assumption/Arithmetic]. OP = \u20ac11.9B mid-point of \u20ac11.8\u201312.2B at cc, with ~0.1B FX drag [Assumption].\n- **2027 revenue and margin**: Management statement \"total revenue growth to accelerate in 2027\" and \"total operating expenses to grow at 80% to 90% of total revenue growth in 2027\" [Actual \u2014 Q2 2026 statement]. 12.9% reported growth (13.5% cc \u2212 0.6pp FX) [Assumption]; margin 30.8% derived: opex grows at 85% of revenue growth \u2192 ~1.5pts margin expansion.\n- **2028\u20132030**: **NO company guidance exists.** These are my [Assumption]: revenue decelerates from +10% to +7.7% (CCB growth 26% today will fade to ~10\u201312% by 2028); margin expands ~0.5pt per year to 32.2% (AI reinvestment partially offsets operating leverage). **This is the largest judgment in the model.**\n- **Economics of FCF**: tax 29% (2026 guidance [Actual]); D&A ~4\u20136% of revenue [Assumption]; capex ~2.5\u20133.2% of revenue [Assumption, consistent with 2025 actual 2.5%]; \u0394WC = modest use of cash (deferred revenue growth partly offset by receivables) [Assumption].\n\n**Step 3-3. DCF calculation (WACC 7.5%, mid-year discounting)**:\n\n| FY | FCF (\u20acB) | Discount factor | PV (\u20acB) |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 2026E | 10.00 | 0.9646 | 9.65 |\n| 2027E | 10.78 | 0.8982 | 9.68 |\n| 2028E | 12.02 | 0.8350 | 10.04 |\n| 2029E | 13.18 | 0.7766 | 10.24 |\n| 2030E | 14.32 | 0.7222 | 10.34 |\n| **Sum PV explicit** | | | **49.95** |\n\n- Terminal growth: **3.0%** [Assumption \u2014 below German nominal GDP long-run ~3.2\u20133.5%; SAP is global, but conservative]\n- Terminal FCF = 14.32 \u00d7 1.03 = 14.75; TV = 14.75 / (0.075 \u2212 0.03) = **\u20ac327.8B**\n- PV of TV = 327.8 \u00d7 0.7222 = **\u20ac236.7B**\n- **EV = 49.95 + 236.7 = \u20ac286.7B**\n- Net debt: vendor net cash $0.87B [Actual \u2014 vendor] \u2248 \u20ac0.75B; add leases \u20ac3.0B [Assumption] \u2192 net debt \u2248 **\u20ac2.25B**\n- **Equity value = \u20ac284.4B**; shares 1,154.2M [Actual \u2014 pack] \u2192 **\u20ac246.4/share \u2248 $287.4**\n\n**Step 3-4. Multiples cross-check**:\n- Base IV $287.4 \u2192 FY2026E P/E = 287.4 / (\u20ac7.32 \u00d7 1.1662 = $8.54) = **33.7\u00d7**; FY2027E P/E = 287.4 / ($10.30) = 27.9\u00d7 \u2014 at the high end of SAP's 20\u201330\u00d7 history, but justified by 2027 acceleration.\n- At market $219.2: FY2026E P/E = 25.7\u00d7 vs mean analyst target +10.8% upside \u2014 market discounts stagnant margin/terminal.\n- EV/Sales FY2026E: at IV $287.4 \u2192 \u20ac286.7B / \u20ac47.1B = **6.1\u00d7**; vs MSFT ~13\u00d7, ORCL ~10\u00d7, CRM ~5\u00d7 [Estimate \u2014 not retrieved at T0, approximate] \u2014 not expensive for a 12\u201313% grower with 86% recurring revenue.\n- PEG: 33.7 / 17.6 = 1.9 at IV; at market 25.7/17.6 = **1.46** \u2014 at market price, PEG is reasonable, not demanding.\n\n**Step 3-X. Tornado sensitivity (Top 3 variables)**:\n\n| Variable | \u22121\u03c3 move | +1\u03c3 move | IV range |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 2028\u201330 revenue CAGR (base 8.8% avg; \u03c3=2pts) | 6.8% \u2192 IV ~$250 | 10.8% \u2192 IV ~$335 | $250\u2013335 |\n| 2030 operating margin (base 32.2%; \u03c3=1.5pts) | 30.7% \u2192 IV ~$264 | 33.7% \u2192 IV ~$310 | $264\u2013310 |\n| WACC (base 7.5%; \u03c3=40bps) | 7.9% \u2192 IV ~$265 | 7.1% \u2192 IV ~$312 | $265\u2013312 |\n\n\u2192 **Top 3 thesis KPIs: CCB growth (drives 2028\u201330 revenue), non-IFRS margin, 10Y Bund yield (WACC).** The market should move on all three.\n\n**Step 3-X. Reverse DCF (market-implied path)**:\nAt $219.2 (\u20ac188.0), equity \u20ac216.9B, EV \u2248 \u20ac219.2B. Holding my explicit 2026\u201327 forecast (\u20ac10.0B, \u20ac10.8B FCF), the residual PV is \u20ac219.2 \u2212 19.3 = \u20ac199.9B; PV factor 0.7222 \u2192 implied TV = \u20ac276.8B; implied terminal FCF = \u20ac276.8B \u00d7 4.5% = **\u20ac12.46B** at a 3% terminal growth \u2014 vs my 2030 FCF of \u20ac14.32B. The market implies **FCF stalls at ~\u20ac12B (\u2248 my 2028 level) for a decade** \u2014 i.e., zero real FCF growth after 2028. Market horizon priced: ~2 years of growth, ignoring the 2027 acceleration and margin expansion. **Feasible but conservative** \u2014 not excessive, not unrealistic.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n\u25a0 SECTION 3.5. SECOND-ORDER EFFECTS\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n\n**Step 3.5-1. Competitive response simulation**: If SAP's Autonomous Enterprise/AI agents gain traction (Q4 2025: Business AI in 2/3 of cloud order entry [Actual]), Oracle will intensify price/feature aggression in Financials/HCM, Microsoft will bundle Dynamics with Azure credits, and LLM-native startups will attack vertical modules. Net impact: **\u22121** (some margin pressure in extension products, contained by clean-core lock-in).\n\n**Step 3.5-2. Reflexivity check**: \nPositive: elevated equity (SBC, M&A currency) attracts AI talent; dominant-customer trust reinforces. Negative: the 2026 price reset (high $281 \u2192 low $145 [Actual \u2014 pack]) created retention questions; magnitude modest given dividend yield 1.41% and buyback. Net: **0**.\n\n**Step 3.5-3. Customer behavior evolution**: Early adopters of RISE are now mainstream: 17,000+ verified customers, 43,338 implementations [Estimate \u2014 ERP Research]. As penetration grows, expansion revenue (net retention) slows; churn risk shifts from \"no cloud\" to \"cloud optimization\" (empty-apartment risk, per bear research [Estimate \u2014 cloud03]). Net: \u22121 to revenue growth in outer years \u2014 already embedded in my 2028\u201330 deceleration.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n\u25a0 SECTION 4. SCENARIO ENGINE (BAYESIAN)\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n\n**Step 4-1/4-2. Scenario composition** (probabilities sum to 100%; Base = single highest):\n\n**Bear \u2014 30% \u2014 IV $217/ADR**:\n- 2028\u201330 revenue +7%/6%/5% (AI disruption + Oracle gains + support revenue decline accelerates); 2030 OM 31.5%; WACC 8.0%; terminal g 2.5% \u2014 derived FCF path: 10.0/10.8/11.4/12.2/12.9, TV \u20ac241B \u2192 IV \u20ac186 \u2248 $217.\n- Interpretation: market currently sits exactly here \u2014 this is not an extreme bear.\n\n**Base \u2014 50% \u2014 IV $287/ADR**:\n- Forecast as in Section 3: CCB converts, total revenue accelerates to +12.9% in 2027, decelerates to +7.7% by 2030; margin rises to 32.2%; WACC 7.5%; terminal g 3.0% \u2192 IV \u20ac246 \u2248 $287.\n\n**Bull \u2014 20% \u2014 IV $403/ADR**:\n- AI platform premium materializes: 2028\u201330 revenue +12%/11%/10%; 2030 OM 33.5% (AI-opex leverage beats plan); WACC 7.0%; terminal g 3.5% \u2192 IV \u20ac345 \u2248 $403.\n- Trigger: CCB growth stays >20% cc through 2027 and AI attach rate in order entry >70%.\n\n**Step 4-3. Bayesian frame (prior \u2192 posterior)**:\n- Prior (from Layer 1.5 base rates): P(successful AI transition) = 45%.\n- Likelihood update from FY2025\u2013H1 2026 data: CCB +26% cc, AI in 2/3 of order entry, non-IFRS OP beat, FCF beat \u2192 likelihood ratio ~1.4\u20131.5.\n- Posterior P(success) \u2248 45% \u00d7 1.45 / (45% \u00d7 1.45 + 55%) \u2248 **54%**. My Base+partial-Bull probability (50% + part of 20%) is consistent: the market's implied P(success) \u2248 40\u201345% (Reverse DCF). I am modestly more optimistic than the market, within the prior-update range \u2014 no overconfidence red flag.\n\n**Step 4-4/4-5. Expected price and MoS**:\n- Expected Price = 0.30\u00d7217 + 0.50\u00d7287 + 0.20\u00d7403 = **$289** [Estimate]\n- 50% CI: **$217\u2013$403** (from the scenario distribution, 25th\u201375th percentile) [Estimate]\n- 80% CI: **$150\u2013$450** [Estimate \u2014 incorporates tail-risk inputs from section 7]\n- Base IV: $287; MoS = (287 \u2212 219.2)/287 = **23.6% \u2192 Adequate** (15\u201330% band)\n- Expected-value MoS = (289 \u2212 219.2)/289 = 24.1%\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n\u25a0 SECTION 4.5. TIME HORIZON ARBITRAGE\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n\n- **Market-implied horizon**: Reverse DCF shows the market prices ~2 years of visible growth and then a perpetual stall (FCF flat at ~\u20ac12B); that is a ~2-year forward horizon.\n- **My horizon**: 3\u20135 years, anchored by (a) CCB already contracts \u20ac22.9B of near-term revenue; (b) management's explicit 2027 acceleration; (c) ECC maintenance deadlines (2027/2030) force S/4HANA migrations.\n- **Spread = 2+ years** \u2192 a genuine horizon arbitrage exists, **provided** execution continues. This is the structural source of the 24% MoS.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n\u25a0 SECTION 5. CONVICTION & POSITION SIZING\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n\n**Step 5-1. Conviction score (0\u20133 per axis, /15)**:\n| Axis | Score | Rationale |\n|---|---|---|\n| Business quality | 3/3 | Fortress moat (17/21), 86% recurring revenue, 22.4% FCF margin |\n| Valuation attractiveness | 3/3 | 24% MoS; market prices a 2-year horizon with a lifetime stall |\n| Macro alignment | 1/3 | Stagflation 40%, high rates, EUR strength \u2014 headwind |\n| Thesis clarity | 3/3 | KPI set fully disclosed: CCB, cloud GM, OP margin, FCF |\n| Execution traceability | 2/3 | 2 consecutive years of guidance beats [Actual]; AI revenue attribution still murky |\n\n**Total: 12/15 \u2192 High.** Apply Layer 1 macro deduction (\u22120.5 step) and Red-Team gap (Section 9, logic gap 1.5 < 2.0 \u2192 further \u22121) \u2192 **Final Conviction: 11/15 \u2014 High (lower band)**.\n\n**Step 5-2. Conviction decay**: \u22121 point every 6 months without confirming evidence. Renewal triggers: Q3/Q4 2026 CCB growth >20% cc, non-IFRS OM \u226529%, cloud GM \u226574%.\n\n**Step 5-3. Sizing guidelines**: High conviction + macro headwind \u2192 **initial 4\u20136%, max 8%** (vs the unconstrained 8\u201312% band). Engine 1 designation avoids the stricter Engine 4/5 caps.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n\u25a0 SECTION 5.5. BEHAVIORAL & POSITIONING\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n\n- **Short interest**: 0.74% of float, 8.55M shares, days-to-cover 2.57, MoM **\u221223.9%** [Actual \u2014 vendor] \u2192 no squeeze, shorts actively covering \u2192 no bearish crowding; mild positive tell.\n- **Institutional ownership**: 7.75% [Actual \u2014 vendor] \u2014 this is 13F ADR-only data and drastically understates global institutional ownership; not a reliable positioning signal. Passive/ETF flows: SAP is a top-20 European index constituent; vulnerable to European-outflow episodes.\n- **Insider activity**: 0.0% insider ownership \u2014 normal for a German SE with two-tier governance; not a signal.\n- **Options positioning**: [Unconfirmed] \u2014 not in pack, not retrieved.\n- **Sentiment**: Price $219 after a $144.97\u2013281.37 range: recovered 44% off the low; analyst mean $242.9 / median $239.5 [Actual \u2014 vendor] \u2014 sentiment is *cautious-neutral*, not euphoric. No contrarian sell signal.\n- **Crowding risk score: 4/15 \u2014 Low.** No reduction in position size.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n\u25a0 SECTION 6. PORTFOLIO FIT\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n\n- Adds a European-currency quality compounder with defensive (86% recurring) cash flows; beta 0.76 [Actual \u2014 vendor] dampens portfolio volatility.\n- Correlation with US growth-tech: ~0.6\u20130.7 [Assumption] \u2014 meaningful but not 1.0; the EUR revenue base provides modest USD-dollar diversification.\n- Best fit in portfolios that are already heavy in US large-cap growth (lowers dollar concentration); weaker fit in stagflation-heavy portfolios (SAP is not a real-asset hedge).\n- Quality increases if the portfolio holds cyclicals/commodities \u2014 SAP's recurring cash flow is a stabilizer.\n- **Fit: Moderate-to-good.** No portfolio-level deduction applied.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n\u25a0 SECTION 6.5. KELLY SIZING\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n\n- Estimate: p(profit over 3-yr) \u2248 65% (Base+Bull weights, some tail-loss inside Bear); average win \u2248 +32% (from $219 to ~$289 expected); average loss \u2248 \u221220% (bear-bear path) [Assumption].\n- Odds b = 32/20 = 1.6. Full Kelly f* = (p\u00b7b \u2212 q) / b = (1.04 \u2212 0.35)/1.6 = **43%** (theoretical maximum).\n- **Half-Kelly \u2248 21%; portfolio cap 10%; macro headwind + Red-Team gap \u2192 cap 8%.**\n- Consistency check Layer 5 vs 6.5: Layer 5 cap = 8%; Kelly-derived cap = 8%; gap = 0% \u2014 no re-analysis required (rule 13 passed).\n- **Recommended: initial 5% \u2014 add 2% upon KPI confirmation \u2192 terminal 7%; hard cap 8%.**\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n\u25a0 SECTION 7. RISKS & CATALYSTS\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n\n**Risks**:\n1. **AI disruption of the integrated ERP suite** (probability 35\u201345%, impact \u221230\u201340%): composable LLM-native apps substitute modular functionality; Oracle/Microsoft agents capture workflows; SAP's \"Autonomous Enterprise\" fails to convert hype \u2192 my Bear scenario.\n2. **Cloud renewal / \"empty apartment\" churn** (probability 30%, impact \u221215\u201320%): customers buy RISE under 3-year contracts but underutilize, then downsize at renewal \u2014 CCB growth falls to single digits in 2028.\n3. **Macro/geopolitical shock** (probability 25\u201335%, impact \u221220%): Middle East escalation, oil spike, stagflation; IT budgets freeze; FX EUR strength persists (guidance assumes 1.13, spot 1.17 \u2014 already costing ~1.5pp growth [Actual]).\n4. **Regulatory/legal**: EU aftermarket-licensing commitments; US price-fixing probe; $222M bribery settlement precedent [Estimate \u2014 research brief; not independently verified] \u2192 compliance costs and pricing limitations (probability 20%, impact \u22125\u201310%).\n5. **Software-support revenue decline accelerates** (currently \u22129% [Actual]): if the decline doubles to \u221215\u201318% and cloud growth fades below 15%, total revenue growth drops below 7%.\n6. **M&A/capital allocation**: Dremio/Prior Labs dilution shows AI-assembly risk; capital could be wasted chasing AI.\n\n**Catalysts**:\n1. **Q3/Q4 2026 earnings**: CCB growth sustaining >22\u201324% cc; non-IFRS OP \u2265 \u20ac12.0B; FCF \u2265 \u20ac10B \u2192 re-rating to $240\u2013260.\n2. **2027 guidance (January 2027)**: management's first explicit 2027 numbers; if total revenue growth guides to \u226512% and margin \u226530%, my Base case is confirmed.\n3. **ECC end-of-maintenance deadlines (2027/2030)** \u2014 industry-level forced-migration catalyst.\n4. **AI monetization metrics**: % of cloud order entry with Business AI >70%; AI attach pricing disclosed.\n5. **Buyback:** \u20ac7.4B remaining through 2027 [Actual \u2014 Q2 release] \u2014 a persistent bid.\n6. **Rates**: if Bunds fall below 3.0%, WACC falls and IV rises ~5\u20138%.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n\u25a0 SECTION 7.5. CORRELATION-ADJUSTED RISK\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n\n- **Common bear triggers with the rest of a growth-heavy portfolio**: 1) US 10Y > 5% \u2192 multiple compression across quality tech; 2) EUR/USD rally toward 1.25 \u2192 EUR-translation drag; 3) AI-led sector rotation out of incumbents toward small-cap LLM names; 4) recession \u2192 IT budget freeze.\n- **Tail correlation**: in the 2022-style stress (rates + inflation), SAP fell ~30\u201340%, close to US tech beta \u2014 correlation at the tail \u2248 0.75\u20130.85 [Assumption].\n- **CVaR (95%)**: expected loss in the worst 5% scenario \u2248 **$150\u2013160/share** (\u221227\u201332%) \u2014 driven by combined AI disruption + macro shock. This matches the 80% CI lower bound.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n\u25a0 SECTION 8. MONITORING RULES & THESIS INTEGRITY\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n\n**Step 7-1. Thesis integrity thresholds**:\n| KPI | Current | Trigger re-evaluation |\n|---|---|---|\n| CCB growth (cc) | +26% | <15% for one quarter or <18% for two consecutive |\n| Non-IFRS operating margin | 27.8% Q2'26 | <27% (quarterly, ex-M&A) |\n| Cloud gross margin (non-IFRS) | 74.6% | <72% |\n| Total revenue growth (cc) | ~11% | <8% |\n| Software-support revenue decline | \u22129% | accelerating past \u221212% |\n| FCF | \u20ac6.25B H1'26 | FY run-rate falling below \u20ac8.5B |\n\n**Step 7-2. Pre-mortem \u2014 \"If the investment failed in 5 years, why?\"**:\n1. **AI bypass** (40%): a portfolio of LLM-native tools replaced the monolithic suite; CCB growth collapsed to <10% by 2028. Early warning: non-AI competitive wins by Oracle/Workday/Salesforce in SAP's installed base; CCB growth falling; AI attach rate stagnating <50%.\n2. **Renewal cliff** (35%): the 2024\u201326 RISE cohort renews at 40\u201350% smaller contracts after \"empty-apartment\" optimization. Early warning: cloud gross margin <72% (discounting to retain); cloud revenue growth falling >5pts faster than CCB.\n3. **Macro/financialization** (25%): stagflation forces IT budget cuts; EUR strengthens to 1.30; Bund yields rise to 4.5% compressing multiples permanently. Early warning: 10Y Bund >3.75%; EUR/USD >1.25; negative annual contract value in mid-market.\n\n**Step 7-3. Decision journal entry**:\n- T0: $219.20 (2026-08-24); IV base $287; expected value $289; key assumptions: 2027 acceleration per management, 2028\u201330 rev CAGR 8.8%, 2030 OM 32.2%, WACC 7.5%, terminal g 3.0%. Bear thesis documented in Section 9. Red-team concerns: AI bypass, empty-apartment churn. Trigger: re-analyze if CCB <15% or OM <27%.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n\u25a0 SECTION 9. RED TEAM & ADVERSARIAL ANALYSIS\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n\n**Step 9-1. Short thesis (using the same data)**:\n1. The LLM stack makes workflow-specific AI tooling cheap to build; SAP's 26% CCB growth is momentum, not proof \u2014 order-entry \"AI attachment\" is marketing bundle, not incremental revenue.\n2. \u20ac22.9B CCB is contracted revenue, but if cloud workloads are underutilized (\"empty apartment\"), 2027\u201328 renewals will be dramatically smaller \u2014 the market is paying 26\u00d7 for a 2-year revenue payday followed by a hangover.\n3. Software-support revenue is in terminal decline (\u22129% and accelerating); the legacy cash cow funding the cloud transition is dying on schedule.\n4. Non-IFRS operating profit \"beat\" is cost discipline (opex 80\u201390% of revenue growth), not pricing power; if cloud growth slows, margins compress \u2014 the 32% 2030 margin target assumes everything goes right.\n5. Oracle is winning HCM/financials deals that SAP used to own; Microsoft's Dynamics-Azure-Copilot stack is a bundle SAP cannot match.\n6. EU regulatory actions (licensing/aftermarket) and the US price-fixing probe could cap support pricing at the worst possible moment; governance blemish from $222M bribery settlement persists.\n7. German/EU enterprise software is late to the AI cycle: Dremio and Prior Labs bolt-ons are a $100M+ dilution admission that internal AI work is behind.\n\n**Step 9-2. Logic combat scoring**:\n- Long logic strength: 8/10 \u2014 CCB is a hard contractual number; margin/FCF beats are actual; guidance quality excellent; base-rate justifications explicit.\n- Short logic strength: 6.5/10 \u2014 all points are plausible, but none is corroborated by hard data in hand; the strongest point (#2) is a theory of renewals, not observed churn; #5 partially contradicted by SAP's Q4 2025 Cloud ERP Suite +32% cc.\n- **Gap = 1.5 < 2.0 \u2192 mandatory Conviction discount applied (already reflected: 12 \u2192 11/15).**\n\n**Step 9-3. Adversarial data check**: No Hindenburg-style report exists on SAP. The most serious adversarial items found: EC commitment process (2026) and the $222M bribery settlement [Estimate \u2014 secondary sources; not independently verified]; Bloomberg article \"SAP users question value for money of AI tools\" [Estimate]. Neither changes the valuation more than \u00b13%.\n\n**Step 9-4. Killed arguments and resurrection conditions**:\n- *Killed*: \"SAP is a legacy software company that will fade like IBM.\" IBM still generates $60B+ revenue with stable FCF; SAP's cloud revenue is already \u20ac21B and growing +26% cc. Resurrection condition: if cloud growth <10% for 2 consecutive years.\n- *Killed*: \"Valuation is too high at 27\u00d7 trailing.\" Trailing includes the FY2025 non-IFRS EPS \u20ac6.15; forward FY26 EPS is \u20ac7.32 \u2192 25.7\u00d7 on a 17.6% EPS grower with 86% recurring revenue. Resurrection condition: if EPS growth consensus falls below 8%.\n- *Killed*: \"Buybacks are destroying value.\" Average repurchase price \u20ac161.16 vs current \u20ac188 and my IV \u20ac246 \u2014 so far, they destroyed value? No \u2014 they bought below intrinsic value and below spot; value accretive by ~15\u201330% per repurchased share. Resurrection condition: if they execute the remaining \u20ac7.4B above \u20ac260 (above my IV).\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n\u25a0 SECTION 10. AUDIT RESULTS (37-point sweep, summary of critical items)\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n\n- **A. Methodology**: Archetype B selected with 3+ reasons (fortress moat, 86% recurring revenue, 22.4% FCF margin, 2 years of guidance beats); Engine 1 appropriate; alternative Engine 4 would over-value optionality and under-value the \u20ac8.2B cash flows \u2014 audited and rejected. Transition check: SAP completed the cloud transition (cloud revenue 57% of total [Actual]); no blended-engine requirement \u2014 documented.\n- **B. Valuation**: No DCF-only conclusion; multiples cross-checked. Terminal growth \u22643% < German nominal GDP; WACC derived transparently; all 2028\u201330 drivers labelled [Assumption]; sensitivity shown (Section 3-X). Reverse DCF included. Pass.\n- **C. Bias**: Recency check (Q2 CCB 26% could flatter): mitigated by using FY2025 full-year actuals (26% cc) and 2026 guidance midpoints (23\u201325% cc). Narrative check: \"Autonomous Enterprise\" marketing is not treated as a revenue driver; AI revenue is only modeled through the macro 26% CCB growth assumption. Overconfidence check: Scenario probabilities (30/50/20) imply a 70% chance the stock beats the market-implied path \u2014 justifiable given the 2-yr horizon arbitrage, but that is the _edge_, not a certainty; conviction capped at 11/15 accordingly. Pass.\n- **D. Consistency**: FX \u2014 all DCF in EUR, USD at 1.1662; guidance FX assumption of 1.13 disclosed as drag. Scenarios are monotonic (bear < base < bull). FCF definition consistent (OCF \u2212 capex). Pass.\n- **E. Narrative**: No \"large long-term potential\" without numbers; every qualitative driver has a quantitative proxy. Pass.\n- **F. Red team**: Executed (Section 9); short vs long gap 1.5 led to conviction deduction. Pass.\n- **G. Data integrity**: Pack's own FY2017 SEC data is stale vs FY2025 company disclosures \u2014 used company disclosures (Tier 1 origin) but flagged. The research brief's \u20ac6.8B cloud and \u20ac9.2B total revenue for Q2 2026 contradict the company's \u20ac6.28B and \u20ac9.878B \u2014 brief figures rejected; company release figures used. Vendor SBC period-unreliable \u2192 [Estimate] range used. Debt components [Unconfirmed] \u2192 net debt approximated and held conservatively. **No single failure requiring recalculation.**\n\n**Audit result: PASS (all critical points satisfied).**\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n\u25a0 SECTION 11. DECISION JOURNAL ENTRY\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n\n- **T0**: 2026-08-24 | Price $219.20 | Base IV $287.4 | Expected value $289 | MoS 23.6% | Conviction 11/15\